      "notes": [
        "Each row is a linear probability regression for the indicated current occupation. Service is the omitted outcome category. Each regression includes the five potential experience terms and the same exogenous controls as Table 1, together with interactions between occupation indicators from the previous two survey waves. Only current main job rows with both lagged occupations observed are included. Histories use the previous two scheduled survey waves, including biennial waves; missing interviews are not skipped.",
        "One observed history pair is omitted with the intercept. Empty history pairs are excluded. History F tests only the occupation history block, conditional on the potential experience instruments and included controls. Full set F and partial R squared refer to all excluded instruments together. Standard errors are clustered by respondent and sampling weights are used. Joint test p values below 0.001 are displayed as <0.001.",
        "These are supplementary prediction checks. They do not implement the full transformed wage model or nonlinear IV estimation in Gibbons et al. (2005). The occupation interactions required by the full thesis wage model are not tested here, and relevance alone does not establish instrument validity.",
        "Presentation reference: Gibbons, Katz, Lemieux, and Parent (2005), Journal of Labor Economics, 23(4), Table B3. DOI: 10.1086/491606. Formatting assistance: Codex; numerical estimates are read directly from the saved Stata exports."
